.TH PS 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
ps \- list the processes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ps
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ps
lists every process, one a line, under a header:
.TP
.B PID
The process's id.
.TP
.B PPID
Its parent's id.
.TP
.B PGID
Its process group.
.TP
.B STATE
.B running
(it can run),
.B sleeping
(blocked in a system call: waiting for input, a child or a timer), or
.B zombie
(it has ended and its parent has not waited for it).
.TP
.B COMMAND
The program's path, then its arguments.
.SH NOTES
There are no options; arguments are ignored. There are no users, times
or memory figures to show.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kill (1),
.BR free (1),
.BR uptime (1)
